# Copy to .env.local if you want image uploading in your own build.
#
# You almost certainly do not need this. The published build ships WITHOUT a
# Client-ID on purpose, so there is no upload button, and the image field asks
# for a web address instead. An artist uploads at imgur.com, which needs no
# account, and pastes the address back. That is what people already do.
#
# A single Client-ID shared by every artist was rejected deliberately. It
# identifies the application rather than a user, so anonymous uploads made with
# it belong to no account, but the registration and the responsibility are the
# owner's: one artist breaking Imgur's rules gets the whole application banned
# and uploads stop working for everybody at once. The daily quota is shared the
# same way. See the README.
#
# If you are building your own copy and want the upload button, register a
# Client-ID at https://api.imgur.com/oauth2/addclient, choosing the option with
# no callback URL. Imgur labels it either "Anonymous usage without user
# authorisation" or "OAuth 2 authorization without a callback URL" depending on
# which version of the form you get. You need only the Client ID that comes
# back, never the Client secret.
#
# The Client-ID is a PUBLIC identifier. It ships in the built bundle and that is
# fine. What it is not is a secret: anyone can read it and spend the daily
# anonymous quota attached to it. If that happens, register a new one and
# rebuild.
#
# Leave it empty and the upload button is simply not shown. Pasting an image
# address keeps working, which is how the gallery was built in the first place.
VITE_IMGUR_CLIENT_ID=
